WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.282
The first query shows the individual Laptop January sale rows.

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:08.337
The second query sums them into one product-month value.

00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:11.727
That one total can be placed into a pivot cell.

00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:18.327
But after aggregation, the individual sale IDs and amounts cannot be recovered from the total alone.

00:00:18.327 --> 00:00:23.567
This is the detail lost by aggregation.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:29.907
A reshape is reversible only when the transformation preserves enough information to reconstruct the source.

00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:35.072
Aggregation, duplicate collapsing, and dropped NULL cells can make the process lossy.

00:00:35.072 --> 00:00:43.172
Validate row counts, keys, totals, and category coverage before assuming a pivot-unpivot round trip preserves

00:00:43.172 --> 00:00:44.265
everything.
